2. ngspice (the ngspice team and contributors)
----------------------------------------------

ngspice (https://ngspice.sourceforge.io/) is the maintained successor
of SPICE3f5. Dune uses release ngspice-47 in two ways.

(a) As the numerical reference. Dune is validated against ngspice-47:
the reference rawfiles of the test corpus (corpus/golden/,
corpus/measure/golden/, corpus/pss/golden/ in the repository) are
outputs of ngspice-47 and are redistributed there as test data.

(b) As a source. The following parts of the engine are derived from
ngspice-47 source files rather than from SPICE3f5, because the feature
does not exist in SPICE3f5 or because Dune follows ngspice's revision
of a SPICE3f5 routine. Paths on the right are relative to the ngspice
source tree (src/); the copyright and author lines are those of the
upstream file headers.

  crates/dune-core/src/bsim3/ (mod.rs, eval.rs, temp.rs, params.rs)
      BSIM3v3.3.0 MOSFET model — spicelib/devices/bsim3/: b3.c, b3ld.c,
      b3temp.c, b3set.c, b3mpar.c, b3cvtest.c, b3acld.c, b3noi.c,
      b3check.c, bsim3def.h. See section 3.

  crates/dune-core/src/sp.rs (and the RF-port parts of devices.rs,
  circuit.rs, matrix.rs)
      S-parameter analysis `.sp` — spicelib/analysis/span.c
      ("Alessio Cacciatori 2021"); spicelib/analysis/cktspdum.c
      ("Copyright 1990 Regents of the University of California.
      Author: 1985 Thomas L. Quarles"); the RFSPICE parts of
      spicelib/devices/vsrc/ and of spicelib/analysis/nevalsrc.c
      ("Author: 1987 Gary W. Ng", "Modified by Alessio Cacciatori").

  crates/dune-core/src/engine.rs (operating-point fallback chain)
      spicelib/analysis/cktop.c — dynamic gmin stepping, true gmin
      stepping and Gillespie's source stepping ("Copyright 1990 Regents
      of the University of California. Author: 1985 Thomas L. Quarles.
      Modified: 2000 AlansFixes. Modified: 2005 Paolo Nenzi -
      Restructured"); spicelib/analysis/optran.c — the transient
      operating point ("Copyright 2019 Holger Vogt  All rights
      reserved. Author: 2019 Holger Vogt. Modified BSD license").

  crates/dune-core/src/bsim1.rs, bsim2.rs (noise)
      spicelib/devices/bsim1/b1noi.c, spicelib/devices/bsim2/b2noi.c
      ("Author: 2003 Paolo Nenzi").

  crates/dune-core/src/trnoise.rs, srcfn.rs (transient noise sources
  TRNOISE and TRRANDOM)
      Grammar and semantics follow spicelib/devices/vsrc/vsrcload.c,
      vsrcacct.c, vsrcpar.c ("Copyright 1990 Regents of the University
      of California. Author: 1985 Thomas L. Quarles. Modified: 2000
      AlansFixes"), frontend/trannoise/1-f-code.c ("Copyright: Holger
      Vogt, 2008") and maths/misc/randnumb.c ("Copyright 2008 Holger
